    ($sg$admin-guide$sg$, $sg$Admin guide: what admins do, step by step$sg$, $sg$Admin$sg$, $sg$admin$sg$, $sg$As an admin you see everything a bookkeeper sees, plus the pages that run the firm: people, hours and money, and the firm's settings. This is the written version of the **Admin tour**, with a routine to follow.

### Take the tour

- It starts by itself once, the first time you sign in as an admin. If you're new to the portal, it opens with the basics first (the five places, search and the **?** menu), so you learn to get around before the admin pages.
- Run it again any time from **?** → **Admin tour**, from **Ctrl+K** (**⌘K** on a Mac) by typing "admin tour", or from **Settings › Help**.
- It opens each admin page in turn and points at it: **HR › Members**, **Team › Hours**, **Reply times**, **Performance**, **HR › Reviews**, **Handbook**, **Team › Ledger review**, **Feedback** and **Inventory**, then **Slate › Review**, **Slate › Manage projects**, **Settings › Firm settings** and **Today**. About two minutes, a little longer with the basics.
- To see what your bookkeepers see, run the **Bookkeeper tour** from **?**. It's the same walk they get. Inside **View as**, it walks that bookkeeper's whole app (Today, Clients, Inbox, Work, Team and HR), read-only; the Inbox, Reviews and Handbook stops show a private placeholder, so a stop with nothing to point at is skipped. See [Bookkeeper guide](#/help/bookkeeper-guide).

If you're also a client's account manager, the **Account manager tour** comes next. See [Account manager guide](#/help/account-manager-guide).

### What only admins see

| Where | What it's for | More |
|---|---|---|
| **HR › Members** | Add staff, set roles, assign clients, give temporary admin access, **View as** a bookkeeper (their whole app, read-only) and check **Last seen** to see exactly what they see and when they were last on | [Staff and access](#/help/staff-management), [Temporary access](#/help/temporary-access) |
| **Team › Hours** | Hours and tasks by person and by client, monthly hours budgets and capacity | [Hours budget](#/help/hours-budget), [Capacity](#/help/capacity) |
| **Team › Reply times** | How fast clients hear back, against the 24-hour goal | [Reply times](#/help/reply-times) |
| **Team › Performance** | Every bookkeeper's score out of 100, as a ranking (bookkeepers see only their own) | [Performance](#/help/performance) |
| **Manage projects** in the Slate sidebar | Rename, archive, trash or restore any project | [Manage projects](#/help/manage-projects) |
| **Review** in the Slate sidebar | Approve or send back staff work that needs review, and each person's on-time rate for the last 30 days | [Task review](#/help/task-review) |
| **HR › Reviews › Team status** | Open and run the quarterly review cycle | [Review cycles](#/help/review-cycles) |
| **HR › Handbook** | Staff policies bookkeepers sign, plus reference policies; who countersigns, each bookkeeper's state and their signed copies; drafts, which the policy approver (Bailley) approves before any admin publishes them | [Staff Handbook](#/help/staff-handbook) |
| **Team › Feedback** | Bug reports and ideas from staff and clients | [Feedback](#/help/feedback-page) |
| **Team › Ledger review** | Ledger review settings: warn or block when a month is marked done unapproved, how much ledger to pull, Smart or Strict duplicate checks, and the vendor watch list | [Ledger review](#/help/ledger-review) |
| **Team › Inventory** | Equipment **Requests**, **Items**, the **Roster** of who's missing what, the staff **Directory** and **Export to Google Sheet** | [Inventory](#/help/tech-inventory) |
| **MGB (internal)** in the left rail | MyGoodBooks' own books, set up like a client. Open to every admin by default; the owner can switch it off for a person in **HR › Members**. Never counted in client numbers | [MGB (internal)](#/help/mgb-internal) |
| **Work › Review board** | Every client's 4th, 14th and 24th month-rhythm tasks for a month on one screen, with close status and the client's people; sort, filter and open any task | [Review board](#/help/review-board) |
| **Slate › Waiting on client** | Every open Ask client request for every client, longest wait first, with **Send reminder**, **Email again** and **Cancel** | [Ask client](#/help/ask-client) |
| **Slate › No team yet** | Clients brought over from Asana with no bookkeeper; open one and click **Assign team** to give it one (they own its parked unassigned tasks, which stay claimable; no email) | [Task lists and projects](#/help/task-lists-and-projects) |
| **Bookkeeper** on a client's Slate list | Click it to change the client's bookkeeper; the old bookkeeper's open tasks there can move too (in-review and private ones stay; no email) | [Task lists and projects](#/help/task-lists-and-projects) |
| **Slate › Recurring** | Recurring task templates: drafts, **Turn on**, previews, **Make due tasks now**, **Missed periods** and the standard close set | [Recurring tasks](#/help/task-templates) |
| **Settings › Firm settings** | **Task templates** (a link to Slate › Recurring), **Client roster** (where new clients are added), **Emails**, **QuickBooks usage**, **Usage stats**, **Audit log** and **Developer tools**, plus the **Late tasks** and **Month rhythm** cards (the three monthly Slate dates, 4th, 14th and 24th by default) | [Settings](#/help/staff-settings), [Usage stats and Developer tools](#/help/admin-insight), [Audit log](#/help/audit-log) |
| **Today** | Every client you can open, which for an admin is all of them, plus birthdays and work anniversaries a month ahead; once the Desk is on, **Mine** or **Everyone** to see every staff member's items | [Today](#/help/home-page), [Desk](#/help/workbench), [Celebrations](#/help/celebrations) |
| **Email** to admin@mygoodbooks.org | Health-check alerts and the weekly digest | [Alerts](#/help/health-alerts), [Weekly digest](#/help/weekly-digest) |

### A routine

**Every day**

1. Work through **Today**: client messages, access and upgrade requests, and clients at risk.
2. Glance at admin@mygoodbooks.org for any **"MyGoodBooks alert:"** email and deal with it first. See [What are the health-check alert emails?](#/help/health-alerts).
3. **Review** in the Slate sidebar (`#/tasks/review`): approve or send back work waiting for you, oldest first. See [How does task review work?](#/help/task-review).
4. **Waiting on client** in the Slate sidebar (`#/tasks/waiting`): anything marked **No reply** needs a call. See [How do I ask a client something from a task?](#/help/ask-client).
5. **Today** may show **N profile photos to edit**: download each, remove the background and replace it on **HR › Members**. See [How do I manage staff profile photos?](#/help/staff-photos).
6. **No team yet** in the Slate sidebar: clients that came over from Asana without a bookkeeper. Open each and use **Assign team** so its tasks have an owner. See [How do client task lists and projects work?](#/help/task-lists-and-projects).

**Every week**

1. Read the weekly digest email.
2. **Team › Reply times**: is anyone falling behind the 24-hour goal?
3. **Team › Hours**: anyone over capacity, or a client over its hours budget?
4. **Team › Feedback**: sort new reports.
5. **Team › Inventory › Requests**: approve or order what's been asked for.

**Every month**

1. **Work › Close**: is every client's month closed? See [Month-end close](#/help/month-end-close).
2. On **Today**, open the **This week** card and confirm pricing milestones. See [Pricing milestones](#/help/pricing-milestones).
3. **Team › Hours**: check each client's hours against its budget. See [Hours budget](#/help/hours-budget).
4. **Settings › Usage stats**: what's used and who's gone quiet.

**Every quarter**

1. Open the review cycle on **HR › Reviews › Team status**. See [How do I run a review cycle?](#/help/review-cycles).

**When it comes up**

- A new client: [New client, start to finish](#/help/new-client-start-to-finish).
- A new hire: [Staff and access](#/help/staff-management) and [New-hire onboarding](#/help/new-hire-onboarding).
- Someone leaving: [Offboarding](#/help/offboarding).

### Good to know

- **View as** is read-only: nothing you do there is saved, and each blocked attempt is recorded in the Audit log along with every start and exit. Your own Settings are read-only while you're viewing as someone. Only real admins can use it. See [Staff and access](#/help/staff-management).
- Staff with temporary admin access see some of these pages but not all, and they have their own **Temporary admin tour** that starts the next time they open the portal while access is active. **Emails**, **QuickBooks usage**, the **Audit log** and money figures stay with admins. See [Temporary access](#/help/temporary-access).
