    ($sg$work-page$sg$, $sg$What's on the Work page?$sg$, $sg$Getting started$sg$, $sg$staff$sg$, $sg$**Work** (in the left rail) is where your own work lives. It has five tabs. The tab is part of the address, so a link such as `#/work/close` opens straight to it:

- **Slate** (`#/work/tasks`): a short summary of your Slate: what's **Late**, what's **Due today**, and your **Next** five tasks, with an **Open Slate** button to the full Slate page. Click a row to open the task, the same way as on the Slate page. The Slate page is the one full Slate, with the groups, filters, right-click, drag, select-many and swipes. See [How do I use my Slate?](#/help/my-tasks). For client lists and projects, use the Slate page too; see [How do client task lists and projects work?](#/help/task-lists-and-projects). If you're on the **Classic tasks page**, or the Slate app is switched off, this tab still shows the full list as before.
- **Notes & SOPs** (`#/work/notes`): the **Notes** and **SOPs** cards that used to sit under Slate, working as before, plus **Handoff summaries**, one short summary per client. See [How do I keep notes on a client?](#/help/notes) and [How do I write or update a client's SOP?](#/help/client-sops).
- **Close** (`#/work/close`): every client's month-end close, month by month, with the automatic QuickBooks checks. See [How do I track month-end close?](#/help/month-end-close).
- **Ledger review** (`#/work/ledger`): **Review a file**. Drop in an exported General Ledger and it's checked in your browser; nothing is saved. See [How does Ledger review work?](#/help/ledger-review).
- **Deadlines** (`#/work/deadlines`): filing deadlines for every client you can see, with **Mark filed** and **Create task**. See [How do I track filing deadlines?](#/help/deadlines).

Admins also have a **Review board** tab (`#/work/review`): every client's 4th, 14th and 24th tasks for a month on one screen. See [Review board](#/help/review-board).

Bookkeepers see their own clients. Admins see everyone's.

In **View as** (admins), Work shows the bookkeeper's tabs read-only. **Slate** is a read-only snapshot of their tasks with private tasks hidden, and nothing on it can be changed or popped out. (It is the full snapshot, not the short summary.)

### Getting there fast

- Press **Ctrl+K** (**⌘K** on a Mac) and type "close" or "deadlines" to jump to a tab.
- Press **q** on any staff page to add a task.
- The number on the **Slate** button in the top bar is your open tasks, with overdue ones in red. Click it to open the Slate page.
- Work › Slate's **Open Slate** button, Today's **Open Slate** link and its **Do next** card open Slate; closes that are late or blocked show under **Clients needing attention** and **Also needs you**.
- If you'd rather land on your Slate summary than on Today when you sign in, pick **Work › Slate** under **Appearance & start page** in [Settings](#/help/staff-settings).
$sg$, array[$sg$work$sg$, $sg$ledger review$sg$, $sg$review a file$sg$, $sg$tasks$sg$, $sg$my tasks$sg$, $sg$notes and sops$sg$, $sg$notes & sops$sg$, $sg$close$sg$, $sg$close tracker$sg$, $sg$month-end close$sg$, $sg$deadlines$sg$, $sg$filing deadlines$sg$, $sg$tabs$sg$, $sg$to do$sg$, $sg$notes$sg$, $sg$sops$sg$, $sg$start page$sg$, $sg$slate$sg$]::text[], 45),
    ($sg$review-board$sg$, $sg$Review board$sg$, $sg$Month-end and recurring work$sg$, $sg$admin$sg$, $sg$**Where:** Work › Review board. Admins only.

The Review board shows every client's month-rhythm work for one month on one screen: the **Check in** (4th), **Send reports** (14th) and **Follow up** (24th) tasks, the month-end close status, and who to contact.

### Columns

- **Client.** The name opens the client. The ▸ arrow opens the client's contacts under the row (see below).
- **Bookkeeper** and **Backup.** From the client's assignments. **Unassigned** means no bookkeeper is set.
- **Main contact.** From the client's organization profile. With no profile contact, the client's first active portal login shows instead. **Not set** means neither exists.
- **Check in**, **Send reports**, **Follow up.** One chip per deadline (the column names follow Settings › Firm settings › Month rhythm). A chip says what state the task is in:
  - **Done · Sierra · Nov 14**: who finished it and when.
  - **Not needed · nothing outstanding**: the system closed it because there was nothing to send.
  - **Ready for review · Sierra**: waiting for an approver.
  - **Late · due Nov 14 · Sierra** (red): past its due date and still open.
  - **Open · due Nov 24 · Sierra**, **Open · waiting on client** or **Open · preliminary month**. Waiting on client and preliminary months are never late.
  - **No task yet**: the rhythm has not made this task for the client.
  - A second line, **Email marked sent · Jesse · Nov 14**, shows when someone used **Mark sent** in the email draft.
  Click a chip to open the task.
- **Close.** The same status as the Close tracker (Not started, In progress, Review, Done, N/A, or **Late**). Click it to open the client's Close tab.
- **Approve.** Reserved for a later step. It shows a dash for now.

Every column header sorts the table; click it again to reverse. Empty values stay at the bottom either way. Your sort is remembered in this browser.

### Filters

- **Month:** last month (the default) or the two before it.
- **Bookkeeper:** one person, or **Unassigned**.
- **Status:** **Has late**, **Any open**, **All three done**, **No task yet**, **Close not done** or **Preliminary reports**.
- **Show test clients:** test clients and MGB (internal) are hidden unless this is ticked.
- **Refresh** reloads the board.

The line under the filters counts the clients shown and how the current deadline is going, for example **62 clients · 14th: 41 done, 21 open** (done includes not needed).

### People (the ▸ arrow)

Opens a row under the client with one **People** list: everyone we contact at the client, from the client's Organization profile and portal logins. Each person shows where they came from (**Main contact**, **Main contact (from org profile, not saved as a contact yet)**, **Contact list** or **Portal login**), plus **Monthly emails**, **Can answer**, **Added by client** and **Opted out**. Inactive logins are dimmed. To change the list, use People to contact on the client's Overview; see [What is a client's organization profile?](#/help/client-org-profile).

### Links

- The address `#/work/review?period=2026-10` opens the board on that month (one of the last three).
- Work › Close has an **Open Review board** button for admins.

### Deadline digest (bell)

If the owner has put you on the digest list, your bell gets one entry per deadline, refreshed every morning: **Send reports for October: 41 of 62 done, 21 open**. It comes back as new when the numbers change. Click it to open the Review board on that month. While only test clients have rhythm tasks the entry starts with **Test clients ·**. Nothing is emailed.

### Email drafts: To and Cc, Open in email app, Mark sent

The draft window on a month-rhythm email task (Draft request, Draft reports, Draft maintenance) gains, for admins:

- **To** chips: from the client's **People** list. The main contact and people with **Monthly emails** start on; everyone else starts off, and anyone who opted out is never preselected. Click a chip to turn it on or off. No chips means the client has no contacts yet: add one under People to contact on the client's Overview.
- **Cc** chips: the bookkeeper and the account manager, on unless it is you. They replace the "Suggested CC" line.
- **Copy draft** copies To, Cc, Subject and the email together.
- **Open in email app** opens your own email app with To, Cc, Subject and the email filled in. If the email is too long for that, the app opens without the body and the body is copied for you: **Body copied. Paste it into the email.**
- **Mark sent** records that you sent it (**Marked sent by you · 2:14 pm**, with **Undo**). It does not complete the task. The Review board chip shows the marker.

Nothing is ever sent from the portal. You send the email from your own email app.
